  "title": "Evidentiality",
  "titleRussian": "Эвиденциальность",
  "description": "Expressing source of information",
  "descriptionRussian": "Выражение источника информации",
  "imageName": "eye.circle",
  "intro": "Evidentiality marks how you know something. DIRECT EVIDENCE: no marker needed (Он пришёл - I saw it). HEARSAY: говорят (they say), по словам + gen (according to), якобы (allegedly), мол (quote marker). INFERENCE: видимо/по-видимому (apparently), похоже (it seems), судя по (judging by), должно быть (must be). REPORTED THOUGHT: дескать (supposedly said). Russian speakers frequently mark information source, especially in formal contexts. Omitting evidentials can imply personal witness or certainty.",
  "rules": [
    "Hearsay: говорят (they say), по словам X (according to X), якобы (allegedly)",
    "Inference: видимо (apparently), похоже (seems), должно быть (must be)",
    "Quote marker: мол (he said that...), дескать (supposedly)",
    "Judging: судя по + dat (judging by), насколько я знаю (as far as I know)"
  ],
  "examples": [
    "Говорят, он уехал. (They say he left., hearsay)",
    "По словам министра, реформы необходимы. (According to the minister, reforms are necessary.)",
    "Видимо, он не придёт. (Apparently, he won't come., inference)",
    "Он, мол, болен. (He's supposedly sick., reported speech marker)"
  ],
